{"skill":{"slug":"stock-earnings-review","displayName":"Earnings Review Agent"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1776424773126,"changelog":"Publish 1.0.3","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"BUSINESS_LOGIC.md","size":7690,"sha256":"69c33c8e11dd3aa3fe4b19b6ccfb6e8b99e0c7a6f097f64c2b8070b13136ab78","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9434,"sha256":"3426993ecb1c2b008acf6d265b564e7287818143e0831598b14c58d0281b8731","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/call_review_api.py","size":4355,"sha256":"049b659b7df7ae51b2268653d4c93db036719c36329db35fe66b0456ebeba0d9","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/common.py","size":7057,"sha256":"c224cbe1726d8b752c71514b88fb0f84d160e4f5e50a6c89db0f5f1495b6d4a9","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/normalize_report_period.py","size":4598,"sha256":"887ce582252508119c5ca59f6cbc6636e3823d993b57ca13ffba9c3ad2b26dac","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/validate_entity.py","size":2629,"sha256":"cf38cd6771b2124a5b1d6f9df1941ddf6d5e3b16a0b1f4950258cbdea8e23e67","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2283,"sha256":"c1b3783e51f63fcb37994b4fe35be6cdfec2bddb8df701ad5e0d62444aaf65c9","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789438503074,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8e6d87d4f1f340f1c6cb78f97dd8b0d1e24c4ddfbed8668e355794b5144f3d81","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8e6d87d4f1f340f1c6cb78f97dd8b0d1e24c4ddfbed8668e355794b5144f3d81","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086697795},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":67,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":10,"checkedAt":1789438503074},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a coherent stock earnings review integration, but users should understand it sends queries to Eastmoney APIs and saves returned report attachments locally.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of EM_API_KEY, authenticated network calls, and sending the user's stock-analysis query to Eastmoney are expected for this integration and are disclosed in the skill documentation.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The only declared dependency is the legitimate Python package httpx, but it is unpinned and the documented install command uses the user's Python environment.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The trigger language is somewhat broad for earnings and financial-analysis requests, and the final response uses remote API content and share links; the instructions are still domain-scoped and do not attempt to override agent safety or session goals.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill creates per-run local output directories and saves API-returned attachments by default, with JSON logs only in debug mode; this is disclosed, but attachment size/type validation and retention controls are limited.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches the artifacts: the skill validates a stock entity, selects a report period, calls an Eastmoney performance-comment API, and returns generated content plus saved attachments.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the Eastmoney API service and are comfortable providing EM_API_KEY. Expect the skill to send your query and stock/report identifiers to that service, save returned PDF/Word or spreadsheet attachments under a local miaoxiang/stock-earnings-review run directory, and possibly leave debug logs if debug mode is enabled. Treat generated links and saved attachments as external content.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Downgraded: normalize_report_period.py is only one support step, while call_review_api.py implements the stated earnings-comment generation flow.\n[LP3] expected: Network access, EM_API_KEY use, and local file writes are purpose-aligned and disclosed, though a tighter explicit permission declaration would improve reviewability.\n[SQP-1] expected: The trigger condition is broad, but it remains limited to company earnings, financial reports, and profitability analysis rather than unrelated tasks.\n[SQP-2] expected: Local attachment saving, optional debug JSON logs, and authenticated external API calls are expected for the workflow and documented, but users should be aware files may remain on disk.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese output and formatting requirements are consistent with the Chinese-language skill instructions and examples, not evidence of unsafe behavior.\n[T09] unexpected: The scanner's attachment-handling concern is valid as a hardening issue: remote base64 attachments are decoded and written without size or file-type validation, but the code does not execute them.\n[T09] unexpected: Remote title, content, and shareUrl are returned without URL or markup validation; this is a user-facing trust-boundary risk, not evidence of embedded malicious instructions.\n[T08] expected: The unpinned httpx dependency is a supply-chain hygiene issue, with no evidence that the package name is malicious or typosquatted.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789438503074}}}}}